      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n`exchangeRate` can change during the waiting period of user's request, which can lead to DoS of the protocol. Users that queue the withdrawal can receive incorrect amount of HYPE tokens.\n\n`exchangeRate` can change after the withdrawal request is queued by the user. When the user queues the withdrawal request using `queueWithdrawal` function, the `hypeAmount` is calculated using current `exchangeRate`. The `hypeAmount` is hardcoded in the withdrawal request. `ExchangeRate` can change during the waiting period and it is not validated during the confirmation of the withdrawal request.\n\nThe reason for that is the `asynchronous` nature of the protocol. Right after the user's withdrawal request, the L1 operation is being pushed to `_pendingWithdrawals` where it waits for the processing. Between the user's call to `queueWithdrawal` and the protocol's call to `processL1Operations` the validator can receive rewards or it can be slashed. Slashing or rewards accrual change the current `exchangeRate`, which will differ from the one used in `queueWithdrawal` function.\n\n```solidity\nfunction queueWithdrawal(uint256 kHYPEAmount) external nonReentrant whenNotPaused whenWithdrawalNotPaused {\n        \n        ...\n\n        // Calculate fee in kHYPE using mulDiv for precision\n        // kHYPEAmount is in 8 decimals\n        uint256 kHYPEFee = msg.sender == treasury ? 0 : Math.mulDiv(kHYPEAmount, unstakeFeeRate, BASIS_POINTS);\n        uint256 postFeeKHYPE = kHYPEAmount - kHYPEFee;\n\n        // Convert post-fee kHYPE to HYPE using StakingAccountant\n        // Both kHYPE and HYPE are in 8 decimals\n        uint256 hypeAmount = stakingAccountant.kHYPEToHYPE(postFeeKHYPE);\n\n        // Lock kHYPE tokens\n        kHYPE.transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), kHYPEAmount);\n\n        // Create withdrawal request\n        _withdrawalRequests[msg.sender][withdrawalId] = WithdrawalRequest({\n            hypeAmount: hypeAmount,\n            kHYPEAmount: postFeeKHYPE,\n            kHYPEFee: kHYPEFee,\n            timestamp: block.timestamp\n        });\n\n        ...\n\n    }\n```\n\nWe can see that `hypeAmount` is being calculated and set in `WithdrawalRequest`.\n\nWhen user confirms the withdrawal, after the waiting period, the `_processConfirmation` function returns the `hypeAmount` calculated in `queueWithdrawal` function.\n\n```solidity\nfunction confirmWithdrawal(uint256 withdrawalId) external nonReentrant whenNotPaused {\n        uint256 amount = _processConfirmation(msg.sender, withdrawalId);\n        require(amount > 0, \"No valid withdrawal request\");\n        require(address(this).balance >= amount, \"Insufficient contract balance\");\n\n        stakingAccountant.recordClaim(amount);\n\n        // Process withdrawal using call instead of transfer\n        (bool success, ) = payable(msg.sender).call{value: amount}(\"\");\n        require(success, \"Transfer failed\");\n    }\n```\n\n`_processConfirmation` returns the `hypeAmount` from the request. The issue is that the exchange rate can be different and this will break the price relation between `HYPE` and `kHYPE`.\n\n```solidity\nfunction _processConfirmation(address user, uint256 withdrawalId) internal returns (uint256) {\n        WithdrawalRequest memory request = _withdrawalRequests[user][withdrawalId];\n\n        // Skip if request doesn't exist or delay period not met\n        if (request.hypeAmount == 0 || block.timestamp < request.timestamp + withdrawalDelay) {\n            return 0;\n        }\n\n        uint256 hypeAmount = request.hypeAmount;\n        uint256 kHYPEAmount = request.kHYPEAmount;\n        uint256 kHYPEFee = request.kHYPEFee;\n\n        // Check kHYPE balances\n        require(kHYPE.balanceOf(address(this)) >= kHYPEAmount + kHYPEFee, \"Insufficient kHYPE balance\");\n\n        // Update state\n        totalQueuedWithdrawals -= hypeAmount;\n        totalClaimed += hypeAmount;\n        delete _withdrawalRequests[user][withdrawalId];\n\n        // Burn kHYPE tokens (excluding fee)\n        kHYPE.burn(address(this), kHYPEAmount);\n\n        // Transfer fee to treasury\n        kHYPE.transfer(treasury, kHYPEFee);\n\n        emit WithdrawalConfirmed(user, withdrawalId, hypeAmount);\n\n        return hypeAmount;\n    }\n```\n\nIn this scenario, the slashing between the queue and process will lead to DoS of the system.\n\nIn the scenario, I will skip the protocol withdrawal fee and I will assume that buffer is satisfied, meaning the buffer is zero or it is less than Alice deposit amount. In order to acknowledge the fees and the buffer, we would have to modify the deposit amount to show the exact numbers. Scenario with fee will still work but the numbers would be harder to follow.\n\n#### When the validator gets slashed before processing the operation\n\n1. Alice deposits 100 `HYPE` and receives 100 `kHYPE`\n2. Alice creates withdrawal request with 50 `kHYPE` with 1:1 ratio, she expects to receive 50 `HYPE` and she will have 50 `kHYPE` left, there will be 50 `HYPE` in the protocol\n3. After the withdrawal is queued, the slashing occurs and now instead of 100 `HYPE` there is 50 `HYPE` in the protocol\n4. Operator calls `processL1Operations` to process Alice withdrawal request and withdraw `HYPE` from validator (this does not revert because the exact amount is being withdrawn from the validator, Alice wants 50 and 50 is all the validator has)\n5. Alice confirms the withdrawal and withdraws full 50 `HYPE` from the protocol\n6. Now there is 0 `HYPE` in the protocol and 50 `kHYPE` total supply controlled by Alice, this prevents new deposits, because when the `stake` function is called, it checks if the `HYPE` price is not zero and in this scenario it will be, so it will revert\n7. Bob tries to stake 10 `HYPE` and it reverts\n\nWe get the price from `HYPEToKHYPE` function.\n\n```solidity\nfunction stake() public payable nonReentrant whenNotPaused whenStakingNotPaused {\n        \n        ...\n\n        // Convert HYPE to kHYPE amount using exchange ratio\n        uint256 kHYPEAmount = stakingAccountant.HYPEToKHYPE(msg.value);\n\n        ...\n\n    }\n```\n\n`HYPEToKHYPE` reverts if price is zero.\n\n```solidity\nfunction HYPEToKHYPE(uint256 HYPEAmount) public view override returns (uint256) {\n        uint256 exchangeRatio = _getExchangeRatio();\n        require(exchangeRatio > 0, \"Invalid exchange ratio\");\n        return Math.mulDiv(HYPEAmount, 1e18, exchangeRatio);\n    }\n```\n\nPrice returned from `_getExchangeRatio` is zero because `totalHype` zero and there is positive total supply of kHYPE token so it will not mint the tokens in 1:1 ratio.\n\n```solidity\nfunction _getExchangeRatio() internal view returns (uint256) {\n        // Calculate total kHYPE supply across all unique tokens\n        uint256 totalKHYPESupply = 0;\n        uint256 uniqueTokenCount = _uniqueTokens.length();\n\n        // Sum up the supply of each unique token\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < uniqueTokenCount; i++) {\n            address tokenAddress = _uniqueTokens.at(i);\n            totalKHYPESupply += IERC20(tokenAddress).totalSupply();\n        }\n\n        // Return 1:1 ratio when no kHYPE has been minted yet\n        if (totalKHYPESupply == 0) {\n            return 1e18; // 1:1 ratio with 18 decimals precision\n        }\n\n        // Calculate total HYPE (in 8 decimals)\n        uint256 rewardsAmount = validatorManager.totalRewards();\n        uint256 slashingAmount = validatorManager.totalSlashing();\n        uint256 totalHYPE = totalStaked + rewardsAmount - totalClaimed - slashingAmount;\n\n        // Calculate ratio with 18 decimals precision\n        return Math.mulDiv(totalHYPE, 1e18, totalKHYPESupply);\n    }\n```\n\nAlso the `exchangeRate` will be incorrect in a scenario, when the validator earns rewards after the user creates the withdrawal request and before the L1 operation is being processed.\n\nLast part of this issue is the consequences for the users. All of the `kHYPE` tokens should have the same value. However when the users create the withdrawal request and the `exchangePrice` changes, the user will receive incorrect amount of tokens.\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nCheck the exchangeRate during the claim. It will provide fair and most up to price.",
      "proofOfConcept": "Please add this test to `test/StakingManager.t.sol` and run `forge test --mt \"test_poc\" -vvvv`.\n\nWe expect to revert with `Invalid exchange ratio` custom error which shows, that the user can't deposit into the contract due to incorrect exchange rate.\n\n```solidity\nfunction test_poc() public {\n        vm.startPrank(manager);\n        stakingManager.setUnstakeFeeRate(0);\n        stakingManager.setTargetBuffer(0);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        uint256 stakeAmount = 1 ether;\n        uint256 withdrawalAmount = stakeAmount / 2;\n        uint256 slashedAmount = stakeAmount / 2;\n\n        vm.startPrank(manager);\n        validatorManager.activateValidator(validator);\n        validatorManager.setDelegation(address(stakingManager), validator);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.deal(user, stakeAmount);\n        vm.prank(user);\n        stakingManager.stake{value: stakeAmount}();\n\n        // Approve and queue withdrawal\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        kHYPE.approve(address(stakingManager), withdrawalAmount);\n        // Store the withdrawalId (should be 0 for first withdrawal)\n        uint256 withdrawalId = 0;\n        stakingManager.queueWithdrawal(withdrawalAmount);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Slash the validator\n        vm.prank(address(oracleManager));\n        validatorManager.updateValidatorPerformance(\n            validator,\n            stakeAmount,\n            8000,\n            7500,\n            9000,\n            8500\n        );\n\n        vm.prank(address(oracleManager));\n        validatorManager.reportSlashingEvent(validator, slashedAmount);\n\n        // Add ETH to the StakingManager contract to process the withdrawal\n        vm.deal(address(stakingManager), withdrawalAmount);\n\n        // Set withdrawal delay to 0 to allow immediate confirmation\n        vm.prank(manager);\n        stakingManager.setWithdrawalDelay(0);\n\n        // Confirm withdrawal - use the actual hypeAmount from the request\n        vm.prank(user);\n        stakingManager.confirmWithdrawal(withdrawalId);\n\n        // Contract is Dosed\n        vm.deal(user, stakeAmount);\n        vm.prank(user);\n        vm.expectRevert(\"Invalid exchange ratio\");\n        stakingManager.stake{value: stakeAmount}();\n    }\n```",
